WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:04.375
Now the compass rose itself, which holds more than it seems to.

2
00:00:04.625 --> 00:00:08.875
The outer ring shows true directions, with zero at true north.

3
00:00:09.125 --> 00:00:12.225
The inner ring shows magnetic directions.

4
00:00:12.475 --> 00:00:16.500
It’s the same circle, twisted by the local variation.

5
00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:22.450
In the center, it tells you the variation, the year it was measured, and the annual change.

6
00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:27.750
Use the rose nearest your work, because variation changes across the chart.

7
00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:30.100
So which ring should you use?

8
00:00:30.350 --> 00:00:32.525
The inner ring looks tempting.

9
00:00:32.775 --> 00:00:35.675
It gives you magnetic with no arithmetic.

10
00:00:35.925 --> 00:00:37.600
What’s the catch?

11
00:00:38.600 --> 00:00:41.100
The rose may be years out of date.

12
00:00:41.350 --> 00:00:47.725
So most captains, and most exam problems, work in true on the outer ring, and convert at the end.
